[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186176049,
      "id": "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9",
      "title": "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8c1007d7-af9c-53b7-ba35-ccf8300da852",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zeros of the function are exactly $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}+n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The vertical asymptotes are exactly $x=n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The range of the function is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "81a09050-a21f-5bd7-aae8-46391315455f",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "1905a0ad-0734-5a65-850d-ee4fc8bf7c05",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "fbb0b7bf-9de8-5eea-8160-c45f50c6f67b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "1905a0ad-0734-5a65-850d-ee4fc8bf7c05"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "23553980-59ca-5b56-923b-b490dca4f093",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "0843e405-c3f7-502e-953c-e0b257bd86c8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "74ddcd7e-4758-53f7-bb18-90a949f05994",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "0843e405-c3f7-502e-953c-e0b257bd86c8"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "cc6588b3-34fa-562e-9c5a-249124c53239",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "44199e56-5575-5ba2-9d6c-1d7dd3b30fab",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7e196bda-6289-553e-862b-89a48af2829b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "7e196bda-6289-553e-862b-89a48af2829b"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176049/tangent.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm\\pi,\\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."
    },
